      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Agriculture remains the heart of Maple Hill, with local farms producing ham meats, turkeys, and even a 75‑acre alpaca farm that hosts educational events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitpender.com/maple-hill",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Families in Maple Hill can trace their roots back to Welsh settlers of the 18th century, a lineage that still thrives in the area’s farms today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitpender.com/maple-hill",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town sits just 33 feet above sea level, typical of North Carolina’s Coastal Plain, yet its modest elevation made the maple grove a prominent landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maple_Hill%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Maple Hill’s diverse community includes descendants of freed slaves who settled after emancipation, contributing to a rich cultural tapestry.",
